Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 11:02:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] A totality oracle's via may name a lint rule

`via: lint <tool>:<rule>` or `via: lint <tool>:<rule> matching "<text>"`
names a rule the project's linter runs as the detector, instead of a test.
The tool names an entry in the config, the rule is the tool's own id, and
the matching text keeps only the findings whose message carries it, since
one rule id carries many patterns. over: still names the set in prose.

A value that begins with lint and does not read in this form is a spec
problem with its line, never taken as a test title; the bullet carries no
enforcement until it is fixed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
